    Version=0.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null;214;-6144,-1392;Inherit;False;149.428;100;Quick
    Vectorize;;0,0,0,0.5019608;to optimize;0;0\nNode;AmplifyShaderEditor.StickyNoteNode,
    AmplifyShaderEditor, Version=0.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null;239;3824,-1168;Inherit;False;609.3154;174.0732;Transform;;0,0,0,0.5019608;changes
    the Control of the Textures Transform/UV Tiling & Offset.$$Simple - Standard,
    just how much the Textures Tile (Affect All Textures).$$Custom - Allows for Custom
    Position inputs for TopBottom & Middle Textures Respectively for Specific Tiling
    & Offset (See \"Seperate Position\" Note for details).;0;0\nNode;AmplifyShaderEditor.StickyNoteNode,
    AmplifyShaderEditor, Version=0.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null;287;3824,-800;Inherit;False;605.8608;219.3687;Include
    In W;;0,0,0,0.5019608;To Fetch 'extra Data' that might be stored in the Normal
    Maps, of which is typically left behind in the standard Triplanar Sampler, and
    stores it in the Alpha/W Channel of the output (Only Applies when 'Normal Map'
    is ON):$$None - Returns 1.$$Alpha - Return the Map's Alpha value.$$Z - Returns
    the Map's Z value.;0;0\nNode;AmplifyShaderEditor.StickyNoteNode, AmplifyShaderEditor,
    Version=0.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null;296;-1616,-3008;Inherit;False;323.2468;155.5042;Separate
    Position;;0,0,0,0.5019608;Due to the fact that different Transform Data can't
    be blended into the same vector without severe Texture \"Stretching\" or Artifacting,
    the Position Data must be Separated for Middle & Normal Poles Respectively;0;0\nNode;AmplifyShaderEditor.StickyNoteNode,
    AmplifyShaderEditor, Version=0.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null;299;480,-1040;Inherit;False;133.5004;100;Vectorized;;0,0,0,0.5019608;to
    Simplify & Optimize;0;0\nNode;AmplifyShaderEditor.StickyNoteNode, AmplifyShaderEditor,
    Version=0.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null;312;3760,-1952;Inherit;False;195.5;100.5;Return
    One In Alpha;;0,0,0,0.5019608;in the event Include Alpha is 'False' Return 1.;0;0\nNode;AmplifyShaderEditor.StickyNoteNode,
    AmplifyShaderEditor, Version=0.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null;367;3824,-1552;Inherit;False;605.585;191.6657;Space;;0,0,0,0.5019608;Selects
    what Space the Textures will be projected to:$$Local - good for single Objects,
    Example: Rock or Grabbable Object$$World - good for Level Geometry Or Mulit-Object,
    Example: Sewer Level Or Cliffs/Rock Formations$$Custom - for Custom Space Position
    or Normals (Uses World if unplugged);0;0\nNode;AmplifyShaderEditor.StickyNoteNode,
    AmplifyShaderEditor, Version=0.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null;368;3824,-1328;Inherit;False;606.7822;127.0792;Precompute
    Weights;;0,0,0,0.5019608;to save on calculations or to use custom Weights.$$NOTE:
    this node is made for typical Triplanar Mapping Weights, so if another type of
    mapping is used could lead to artifact or unintended results.;0;0\nNode;AmplifyShaderEditor.StickyNoteNode,
    AmplifyShaderEditor, Version=0.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null;372;3824,-960;Inherit;False;613.1624;132.3754;Normal
    Map;;0,0,0,0.5019608;Applies Normal Tangent Correction, & processes/Unpackes
    the Textures as Normal Maps.$$Note: if there is extra Data in the Z OR Alpha/W
    of the Textures that is needed, Use 'Include In W' Option to Fetch this Data.;0;0\nNode;AmplifyShaderEditor.StickyNoteNode,
    AmplifyShaderEditor, Version=0.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null;373;3824,-544;Inherit;False;610.1477;496.1693;Mirror
    Options;;0,0,0,0.5019608;Options that affect the UVs of the Textures by having
    face or Project in the same way as they do on the otherside of the object.$$Note:
    by default (without prior modification) typical Space Pos UVs naturally mirror,
    as a result the Selection in the Mirror Option is only Vector that ISN'T being
    corrected by the Normal Sign value, I.E.: TopBottom Mirror Option \"X Axis\"
    = XZ Pos * ( 1, NormSign.Y ). $$For More Details See \"TopBot Mirror Switches\",
    \"Middle Mirror Switches\", & \"Swizzle Madness\" Notes.;0;0\nNode;AmplifyShaderEditor.StickyNoteNode,
    AmplifyShaderEditor, Version=0.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null;374;-4304,-1104;Inherit;False;293.2739;157.949;TopBot
    Mirror Switches;;0,0,0,0.5019608;Input for external Switches to control the Top
    & Bottom Texture Mirroring (Expected Values 0 OR 1).$$XY - for Top & Bottom Axis
    Mirroring (for XZ Position Respectively).;0;0\nNode;AmplifyShaderEditor.StickyNoteNode,
    AmplifyShaderEditor, Version=0.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null;386;-1152,-3104;Inherit;False;348.0964;203.7786;Texture
    Space Pos UVs Key;;0,0,0,0.5019608;Key to understand what Axis of the Space Pos
    each Texture uses for their UVs.$$Both Top & Bottom - XZ Position$$Middle (Left
    & Right) - ZY Position$$Middle (Front & Back) - XY Position;0;0\nNode;AmplifyShaderEditor.StickyNoteNode,
    AmplifyShaderEditor, Version=0.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null;413;-1920,-3328;Inherit;False;198.4093;113.5725;Tiling;;0,0,0,0.5019608;a
    Simple approach to Tiling the Textures tho individual control per sample;0;0\nNode;AmplifyShaderEditor.StickyNoteNode,
    AmplifyShaderEditor, Version=0.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null;415;-1680,-1904;Inherit;False;307.4257;217.3511;Middle
    Mirror Switches;;0,0,0,0.5019608;Input for external Switches to control the Middle
    Texture Mirroring (Expected Values 0 OR 1).$$XY - for Front & Back Axis Mirroring
    (for ZY Position Respectively).$$ZW - for Left & Right Axis Mirroring (for XY
    Position Respectively).;0;0\nNode;AmplifyShaderEditor.StickyNoteNode, AmplifyShaderEditor,
    Version=0.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null;416;-1968,-1648;Inherit;False;288;290;Swizzle
    Madness;;0,0,0,0.5019608;tho this looks like a LOT of Nonsense, just keep in
    mind this is just shifting the Sign masks to NOT be Applied to Target Vector
    of the Mirror Option (See Mirror Options for details).$$TopBot Sign Key:$X =
    NormSign.Y$Y = 1$$Middle Sign Key:$X = NormSign.X$Y = 1$Z = -NormSign.Z$;0;0\nNode;AmplifyShaderEditor.StickyNoteNode,
    AmplifyShaderEditor, Version=0.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null;419;-2112,-2976;Inherit;False;242.8517;182.3127;Middle
    Pos 'W';;0,0,0,0.5019608;this is for a Seperate Y component for Left & Right
    Sample tho if there is no intended Difference for either Sample, then Swizzle
    the Pos as such: $$' SpacePos.XYZY '.;0;0\nNode;AmplifyShaderEditor.StickyNoteNode,
    AmplifyShaderEditor, Version=0.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null;421;-7376,-4224;Inherit;False;530.0786;183.1801;Credits
    & Sources;;1,0,0,0.5019608;Triplanar Method Provided By: ASE$$ASE Method Source:
    Pulled from The Triplanar Sampler node's code (plug a single node by itself into
    a blank shader, compile and then \"Open in Text Editor\")$$Node Created by: Tiber
    Legacy;0;0\nNode;AmplifyShaderEditor.StickyNoteNode, AmplifyShaderEditor, Version=0.0.0.0,
    Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null;422;2592,-928;Inherit;False;316.4805;126.8949;Normal
    Tanget Correction;;0,0,0,0.5019608;Sited by ASE's Wiki \"so that tangent space
    vectors from normal maps align correctly onto the object surface, otherwise normal
    maps will look inverted in some projection planes.\";0;0\nNode;AmplifyShaderEditor.StickyNoteNode,
    AmplifyShaderEditor, Version=0.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null;428;-336,-224;Inherit;False;194;192;Normal
    Scale;;0,0,0,0.5019608;Scales the Strength of the Unpacked Texture Normals.$$Key:$X
    for Top Normal$Y for Middle Normal$Z for Bottom Normal;0;0\nNode;AmplifyShaderEditor.StickyNoteNode,
    AmplifyShaderEditor, Version=0.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null;461;-336,-1296;Inherit;False;281.8123;119.8818;2
